 "strategy": "The first tokens of the body and the end of the answer. Compare, for about 40 practice prompts, the logits `u` at the positions that produce the first few body tokens with the tokens of the reference solutions (one trace run): which tokens does the model rank too high or too low, systematically across prompts (for example a habit of starting with one statement form, or of never stopping)? Then act on the output side: the E row of a token decides both how it is read and how likely it is written, and the last layer's W2 and Wo columns decide what is pushed at the end. Small, targeted changes to a handful of rows or columns (a few int8 steps) that correct a systematic bias; also look at answers that run on after the function is complete or that end too early, and at the line-break and end-of-text tokens.",
